 <212658678+luuoaoa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 12:46:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [PoC] Routing probe: Vietnamese keys bypass the mojo IME on
 device
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On-device result from deploying the PoC ash-chrome to a crosvm instance and
driving it with real evdev keystrokes: typing "congas "/"windows " yields the
mangled "congá "/"windớ ", i.e. NOT UnikeyEngine's "congas"/"windows". So the
vendored engine is not what serves physical Vietnamese keys.

Instrumenting the running binary (verified via /proc/<pid>/exe to be this build)
showed why: NativeInputMethodEngineObserver::OnActivate never fires across IME
switches, the connection factory's ConnectToInputMethod never fires, and no
ImeService utility process is spawned at all. The Google Input Tools component
extension serves vkd_vi_telex entirely in JavaScript; the C++ mojo IME path is
dead for physical typing. This confirms VIETNAMESE-IME.md §9 end-to-end.

Consequence for the port: the real step-0 routing fix is deeper than a Chrome
observer tweak -- it needs input-method registration/allowlisting so ash routes
vkd_vi_* to the first-party NativeInputMethodEngine + mojo path (which also spawns
ImeService), or replaces the extension's Vietnamese handling OS-side. The widening
of IsRuleBasedEngine here is kept as a correct-in-principle partial, but on its own
has no effect because the observer is bypassed; comment says so. Diagnostic
LOG(ERROR) lines removed after use.

VERIFIED clean compile of ime:lib and the input_method target. VM instance 2
(owner imepoc) released; 0/1 untouched.



---
 .../native_input_method_engine_observer.cc     | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ash/input_method/native_input_method_engine_observer.cc b/chrome/browser/ash/input_method/native_input_method_engine_observer.cc
index 172c7b5502..f8d10d5295 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ash/input_method/native_input_method_engine_observer.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ash/input_method/native_input_method_engine_observer.cc
@@ -65,7 +65,18 @@ struct InputFieldContext {
 };
 
 bool IsRuleBasedEngine(std::string_view engine_id) {
-  return base::StartsWith(engine_id, "vkd_", base::CompareCase::SENSITIVE);
+  // colorburst PoC note (routing / step 0): also match a fully-qualified
+  // component id embedding a "vkd_" layout. This was an attempt to force
+  // Vietnamese onto the in-process mojo engine. It is INSUFFICIENT on its own:
+  // on-device diagnosis (VIETNAMESE-IME-PERF.md 5.2) showed this observer is
+  // never invoked for vkd_vi_telex -- the Google Input Tools component
+  // extension serves those keys entirely in JS and the ImeService utility
+  // process is never even spawned. The real step-0 fix lives in input-method
+  // registration/allowlisting (make ash route vkd_vi_* to the first-party
+  // NativeInputMethodEngine + mojo path), not here. Kept as a harmless,
+  // correct-in-principle widening of the match.
+  return base::StartsWith(engine_id, "vkd_", base::CompareCase::SENSITIVE) ||
+         engine_id.find("vkd_vi_telex") != std::string_view::npos;
 }
 
 bool IsFstEngine(std::string_view engine_id) {
@@ -134,6 +145,11 @@ std::string NormalizeRuleBasedEngineId(std::string_view engine_id) {
   if (base::StartsWith(engine_id, "vkd_", base::CompareCase::SENSITIVE)) {
     return base::StrCat({"m17n:", engine_id.substr(4)});
   }
+  // colorburst PoC: handle a fully-qualified component id embedding "vkd_".
+  const size_t pos = engine_id.find("vkd_");
+  if (pos != std::string_view::npos) {
+    return base::StrCat({"m17n:", engine_id.substr(pos + 4)});
+  }
   return std::string(engine_id);
 }
 
